  "result": "I graded `submissions/s2.json` and wrote `grades/0001-s2.json`. Three items were correct, two partial and one wrong.\n\n- **q1, q2, q5: correct.** You have the loop, the model's output being only a tool request, and the tool result going back as the next input.\n- **q3: wrong (M6).** You picked \"left to run longer, it will eventually fix it\". An agent that gets the same failing result each step needs a stopping condition, such as a step limit.\n- **q4: partial (M4).** Your 4 is right, but your reason says the model runs the tools. The program runs them. The model only requests one per call.\n- **q6: partial.** The name is only part of what the model reads. It chooses a tool from the description and parameters the program gives it.\n\nI also wrote `review-records/0001-s2-grade.md` and `learning-records/0003-model-requests-program-runs.md`, and updated `NOTES.md`. I did not grade `s1`.\n\n**Next step:** redo q3, q4 and q6 from memory. Then write a one-sentence description for each makerspace tool, and pick a step limit for the assistant.\n\nDo you want a short practice quiz on stopping conditions, who runs the tools, and how the model picks a tool from its description?",
